          "2": "Struggles to break down problems. Solutions are often hacky or short-sighted. Poor understanding of system interactions. Frequent reliance on others for basic debugging. Design docs are missing or unclear.",
          "1": "Unable to solve assigned problems without hand-holding. Solutions introduce new issues. No understanding of architecture. Fails to debug even with guidance."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "delivery_impact",
        "name": "Delivery & Business Impact",
        "weight": 0.20,
        "description": "Reliability in delivering value, meeting deadlines, and aligning work with business goals.",
        "criteria": {
          "5": "Consistently delivers high-impact features ahead of schedule. Proactively identifies opportunities to improve product or efficiency. Work directly drives key business metrics. Manages scope and risks effectively. Unblocks others to accelerate delivery.",
          "4": "Delivers features on time and within scope. Work aligns with team goals and provides clear value. Reliable estimator. Communicates progress and risks proactively. Handles scope changes gracefully.",
          "3": "Delivers most work on time but occasionally misses deadlines or requires scope reduction. Impact is clear but limited to assigned tasks. Estimation accuracy varies. Communication on status is reactive.",
          "2": "Frequently misses deadlines or delivers incomplete work. Impact is unclear or misaligned with priorities. Poor estimation leads to planning issues. Fails to communicate blockers until late stages.",
          "1": "Rarely delivers working software. Work is consistently late or abandoned. No alignment with business goals. Causes delays for the entire team."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "collaboration",
        "name": "Collaboration & Communication",
        "weight": 0.15,
        "description": "Effectiveness in working with cross-functional teams, code reviews, documentation, and knowledge sharing.",
        "criteria": {
          "5": "Fosters a culture of collaboration and psychological safety. Code reviews are educational and empathetic. Documentation is comprehensive and kept up-to-date. Actively shares knowledge via talks, wikis, or pair programming. Bridges gaps between engineering and other functions.",
          "4": "Collaborates effectively with peers and stakeholders. Provides constructive, timely code reviews. Writes clear documentation for features and APIs. Communicates technical concepts to non-technical audiences well. Participates actively in team ceremonies.",
          "3": "Works well in pair or small groups but may be siloed. Code reviews are functional but lack depth. Documentation is adequate but may be outdated. Communication is clear but may lack proactivity. Responsive to requests.",
          "2": "Collaboration is inconsistent. Code reviews are delayed or unhelpful. Documentation is missing. Communication is poor or unclear. Struggles to work with cross-functional partners. Knowledge is hoarded.",
          "1": "Disruptive to team dynamics. Refuses to collaborate or share knowledge. Code reviews are hostile or ignored. No documentation. Communication breakdowns cause project failures."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "growth_mentorship",
        "name": "Growth, Mentorship & Initiative",
        "weight": 0.10,
        "description": "Commitment to personal development, mentoring others, and taking ownership beyond immediate tasks.",
        "criteria": {
          "5": "Actively mentors multiple engineers and elevates team capability. Seeks out stretch assignments and drives initiatives without direction. Provides actionable feedback to peers. Continuous learner who applies new skills to benefit the team.",
          "4": "Open to feedback and actively works on development goals. Mentors junior engineers when asked. Takes ownership of features end-to-end. Learns new technologies relevant to the role. Contributes to team improvement efforts.",
          "3": "Accepts feedback but may not always act on it. Development goals are vague or untracked. Limited mentorship activity. Learns new skills but application is slow. Focuses primarily on own tasks.",
          "2": "Resistant to feedback. No clear development plan. Unwilling to help others. Stagnant skill set. Requires constant direction to stay on track.",
          "1": "Hostile to feedback. No growth mindset. Actively hinders others' growth. Refuses to learn or adapt."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "reliability_ops",
        "name": "Operational Excellence & Reliability",
        "weight": 0.10,
        "description": "Responsibility for system health, incident response, monitoring, and on-call performance.",
        "criteria": {
          "5": "Champions reliability culture. Designs systems with observability and resilience by default. Resolves incidents rapidly and leads effective post-mortems with actionable follow-ups. Proactively reduces toil and improves SLOs.",
          "4": "Maintains system health effectively. Responds to incidents professionally and resolves them within SLAs. Participates in post-mortems and implements fixes. Monitors dashboards and alerts appropriately.",
          "3": "Handles on-call duties adequately but may miss alerts or escalate prematurely. Post-mortem actions are sometimes incomplete. Monitoring is basic. Reactive rather than proactive regarding reliability.",
          "2": "Poor on-call performance. Misses critical alerts. Blames others during incidents. Fails to implement post-mortem actions. Systems lack basic monitoring.",
          "1": "Causes incidents due to negligence. Ignores on-call responsibilities. No monitoring. Refuses to participate in incident response."
        }
      }
    ],
    "evaluation_guide": {
      "instructions": [
        "Review artifacts: Code commits, PRs, design docs, tickets, and incident reports.",
        "Gather feedback: Solicit input from peers, managers, and stakeholders.",
        "Self-assessment: Have the engineer complete a self-review using this rubric.",
        "Calibration: Discuss ratings with other managers to ensure consistency.",
        "Documentation: Provide specific examples for each rating to support the evaluation.",
        "Focus on growth: Use the review to set actionable goals for the next period."
      ],
      "weighting_note": "Weights are suggestions. Adjust based on role level (e.g., increase 'Mentorship' weight for Senior+ roles, increase 'Craftsmanship' for Junior roles).",
      "scoring_formula": "Weighted Score = Sum(Dimension Score * Dimension Weight). Final Rating should reflect holistic judgment, not just the numeric score."
    }
  }
